{"entries":[{"id":"tsk-deu-6-1","title":"Deuteronomy 6:1","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"DEU","chapterStart":6,"verseStart":1,"chapterEnd":6,"verseEnd":1},"content":"<p>1 The end of the law is obedience. 3 An exhortation thereto. 20 What they are to teach their children.</p>\n<p>the commandments. 4:1,5,14,45; 5:31; 12:1; Le 27:34; Nu 36:13; Eze 37:24 go to possess it. Heb. pass over.</p>"},{"id":"tsk-deu-6-2","title":"Deuteronomy 6:2","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"DEU","chapterStart":6,"verseStart":2,"chapterEnd":6,"verseEnd":2},"content":"<p>fear. 4:10; 10:12,13,20; 13:4; Ge 22:12; Ex 20:20; Job 28:28; Ps 111:10 Ps 128:1; Pr 16:6; Ec 12:13; Lu 12:5; 1Pe 1:17 and thy son. 7; Ge 18:19; Ps 78:4-8 thy days. 4:40; 5:16,33; 22:7; Pr 3:1,2,16; 1Pe 3:10,11</p>"},{"id":"tsk-deu-6-3","title":"Deuteronomy 6:3","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"DEU","chapterStart":6,"verseStart":3,"chapterEnd":6,"verseEnd":3},"content":"<p>and observe. 4:6; 5:32; Ec 8:12; Isa 3:10 that ye may. Ge 12:2; 13:16; 15:5; 22:17; 26:4; 28:14; Ex 1:7; Ac 7:17 in the land. Ex 3:8</p>"},{"id":"tsk-deu-6-4","title":"Deuteronomy 6:4","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"DEU","chapterStart":6,"verseStart":4,"chapterEnd":6,"verseEnd":4},"content":"<p>{Shema Yisra�l, Yehowah, Elohainoo, Yehowah aichod,} \"Hear, Israel, Jehovah, our God,is one Jehovah.\" On this passage the Jews lay great stress; and it is one of the four passages which they write on their phylacteries: On the word {Elohim,} Simeon Ben Joachi says: \"Come and see the mystery of the word {Elohim:} there are three degrees, and each degree is by itself alone, and yet they are all one, and joined together in one, and are not divided from each other.\"</p>\n<p>the Lord, 4:35,36; 5:6; 1Ki 18:21; 2Ki 19:5; 1Ch 29:10; Isa 42:8; 44:6,8 Isa 45:5,6; Jer 10:10,11; Mr 12:29-32; Joh 17:3; 1Co 8:4-6 1Ti 2:5</p>"},{"id":"tsk-deu-6-5","title":"Deuteronomy 6:5","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"DEU","chapterStart":6,"verseStart":5,"chapterEnd":6,"verseEnd":5},"content":"<p>thou shalt. 10:12; 11:13; 30:6; Mt 22:37; Mr 12:30,33; Lu 10:27; 1Jo 5:3 God with all. 4:29; 2Ki 23:25; Mt 10:37; Joh 14:20,21; 2Co 5:14,15</p>"},{"id":"tsk-deu-6-6","title":"Deuteronomy 6:6","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"DEU","chapterStart":6,"verseStart":6,"chapterEnd":6,"verseEnd":6},"content":"<p>shall be. 11:18; 32:46; Ps 37:31; 40:8; 119:11,98; Pr 2:10,11; 3:1-3,5; 7:3 Isa 51:7; Jer 31:33; Lu 2:51; 8:15; 2Co 3:3; Col 3:16; 2Jo 1:2</p>"},{"id":"tsk-deu-6-7","title":"Deuteronomy 6:7","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"DEU","chapterStart":6,"verseStart":7,"chapterEnd":6,"verseEnd":7},"content":"<p>And thou shalt. 2; 4:9,10; 11:19; Ge 18:19; Ex 12:26,27; 13:14,15; Ps 78:4-6 Eph 6:4 teach. Heb. whet, or sharpen. shalt talk. Ru 2:4,12; 4:11; Ps 37:30; 40:9,10; 119:46; 129:8; Pr 6:22; 10:21 Pr 15:2,7; Mal 3:16; Mt 12:35; Lu 6:45; Eph 4:29; Col 4:6; 1Pe 3:15</p>"},{"id":"tsk-deu-6-8","title":"Deuteronomy 6:8","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"DEU","chapterStart":6,"verseStart":8,"chapterEnd":6,"verseEnd":8},"content":"<p>11:18; Ex 13:9,16; Nu 15:38,39; Pr 3:3; 6:21; 7:3; Mt 23:5; Heb 2:1</p>"},{"id":"tsk-deu-6-9","title":"Deuteronomy 6:9","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"DEU","chapterStart":6,"verseStart":9,"chapterEnd":6,"verseEnd":9},"content":"<p>11:20; Ex 12:7; Job 19:23-25; Isa 30:8; 57:8; Hab 2:2</p>"},{"id":"tsk-deu-6-10","title":"Deuteronomy 6:10","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"DEU","chapterStart":6,"verseStart":10,"chapterEnd":6,"verseEnd":10},"content":"<p>land. Ge 13:15-17; 15:18; 26:3; 28:13 great. Jos 24:13; Ne 9:25; Ps 78:55; 105:44</p>"},{"id":"tsk-deu-6-11","title":"Deuteronomy 6:11","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"DEU","chapterStart":6,"verseStart":11,"chapterEnd":6,"verseEnd":11},"content":"<p>when thou. 7:12-18; 8:10-20; 32:15; Jud 3:7; Pr 30:8,9; Jer 2:31,32 Eze 16:10-20; Mt 19:23,24</p>"},{"id":"tsk-deu-6-12","title":"Deuteronomy 6:12","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"DEU","chapterStart":6,"verseStart":12,"chapterEnd":6,"verseEnd":12},"content":"<p>bondage. Heb. bondmen, or servants. 12</p>"},{"id":"tsk-deu-6-13","title":"Deuteronomy 6:13","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"DEU","chapterStart":6,"verseStart":13,"chapterEnd":6,"verseEnd":13},"content":"<p>fear. 2; 5:29; 10:12,20; 13:4; Mt 4:10; Lu 4:8 and serve him.Our Saviour quotes these words thus: \"And him only [aut� mon�,] shalt thou serve;\" from which it would appear, that the word {levaddo} was anciently in the Hebrew text, as it was in the Septuagint, Coptic, Vulgate (illi soli), and Anglo-Saxon. Dr. Kennicott argues that without the word only, the text would not have conclusive for the purpose for which our Lord advanced it. It is proper, however, to observe, that the word {levaddo} is not found in any MS. yet collated, though retained in the above versions.</p>\n<p>shalt swear. Le 19:12; Jos 2:12; Ps 15:4; 63:11; Isa 45:23; 65:16; Jer 4:2; 5:2,7 Jer 12:16</p>"},{"id":"tsk-deu-6-14","title":"Deuteronomy 6:14","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"DEU","chapterStart":6,"verseStart":14,"chapterEnd":6,"verseEnd":14},"content":"<p>not go. 8:19; 11:28; Ex 34:14-16; Jer 25:6; 1Jo 5:21 of the gods. 13:7</p>"},{"id":"tsk-deu-6-15","title":"Deuteronomy 6:15","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"DEU","chapterStart":6,"verseStart":15,"chapterEnd":6,"verseEnd":15},"content":"<p>is a jealous. 4:24; Ex 20:5; Am 3:2; 1Co 10:22 lest. 7:4; 11:17; Nu 32:10-15; 2Ch 36:16; Ps 90:7,11 destroy. Ge 7:4; Ex 32:12; 1Ki 13:34; Am 9:8</p>"},{"id":"tsk-deu-6-16","title":"Deuteronomy 6:16","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"DEU","chapterStart":6,"verseStart":16,"chapterEnd":6,"verseEnd":16},"content":"<p>tempt. Mt 4:7; Lu 4:12 tempted him. Ex 17:2,7; Nu 20:3,4,13; 21:4,5; Ps 95:8,9; 1Co 10:9; Heb 3:8,9</p>"},{"id":"tsk-deu-6-17","title":"Deuteronomy 6:17","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"DEU","chapterStart":6,"verseStart":17,"chapterEnd":6,"verseEnd":17},"content":"<p>1,2; 11:13,22; Ex 15:26; Ps 119:4; 1Co 15:58; Tit 3:8; Heb 6:11 2Pe 1:5-10; 3:14</p>"},{"id":"tsk-deu-6-18","title":"Deuteronomy 6:18","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"DEU","chapterStart":6,"verseStart":18,"chapterEnd":6,"verseEnd":18},"content":"<p>shalt do. 8:11; 12:25,28; 13:18; Ex 15:26; Ps 19:11; Isa 3:10; Eze 18:5,19,21 Eze 18:27; 33:14,16,19; Ho 14:9; Joh 8:29; Ro 12:2 that it may. 4:40; 5:29,33</p>"},{"id":"tsk-deu-6-19","title":"Deuteronomy 6:19","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"DEU","chapterStart":6,"verseStart":19,"chapterEnd":6,"verseEnd":19},"content":"<p>Ex 23:28-30; Nu 33:52,53; Jud 2:1-3; 3:1-4</p>"},{"id":"tsk-deu-6-20","title":"Deuteronomy 6:20","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"DEU","chapterStart":6,"verseStart":20,"chapterEnd":6,"verseEnd":20},"content":"<p>when thy son. 7; Ex 12:26; 13:14; Jos 4:6,7,21-24; Pr 22:6 in time to come. Heb. to-morrow.</p>"},{"id":"tsk-deu-6-21","title":"Deuteronomy 6:21","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"DEU","chapterStart":6,"verseStart":21,"chapterEnd":6,"verseEnd":21},"content":"<p>We were. 5:6,15; 15:15; 26:5-9 See on Ex 20:2; Ne 9:9,10; Ps 136:10-12; Isa 51:1; Jer 32:20,21 Ro 6:17,18; Eph 2:11,12 with a mighty. Ex 3:19; 13:3</p>"},{"id":"tsk-deu-6-22","title":"Deuteronomy 6:22","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"DEU","chapterStart":6,"verseStart":22,"chapterEnd":6,"verseEnd":22},"content":"<p>shewed. 4:34; Ex 7:1-12:51; 14:1-31; Ps 135:9 sore. Heb. evil. before. 1:30; 3:21; 4:3; 7:19; Ps 58:10,11; 91:8</p>"},{"id":"tsk-deu-6-23","title":"Deuteronomy 6:23","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"DEU","chapterStart":6,"verseStart":23,"chapterEnd":6,"verseEnd":23},"content":"<p>to give us. 10,18; 1:8,35 See on Ex 13:5</p>"},{"id":"tsk-deu-6-24","title":"Deuteronomy 6:24","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"DEU","chapterStart":6,"verseStart":24,"chapterEnd":6,"verseEnd":24},"content":"<p>to fear. 2 for our good. 10:13; Job 35:7,8; Pr 9:12; Isa 3:10; Jer 32:39; Mt 6:33 Ro 6:21,22 he might. 4:1,4; 8:1,3; Ps 41:2; 66:9; Pr 22:4; Ro 10:5</p>"},{"id":"tsk-deu-6-25","title":"Deuteronomy 6:25","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"DEU","chapterStart":6,"verseStart":25,"chapterEnd":6,"verseEnd":25},"content":"<p>24:13; Le 18:5; Ps 106:30,31; 119:6; Pr 12:28; Eze 20:11 Lu 10:28,29; Ro 10:3,5,6; Ga 3:12; Jas 2:10</p>"}]}